<title>USA: URS wins $18 mln contract.</title>
<headline>URS wins $18 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>URS Corp said on Tuesday it won a three-year contract to provide architectural and engneering services for the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers' seismic risk-mitigation program.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the contract had a maximum value of $18 million if all of the options are exercised.</p>
<p>URS will perform seismic assessments of buildings owned or leased by the federal government. Most of the facilities are Army and Air Force bases throughout the United States.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
</text>
